* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
# Measured on the 2026-10-20 exact-SHA run: apps/observer/start-observer.cmd is stored LF, and a Linux
# checkout with `* text=auto` materialises those LF bytes verbatim, so the one-click launcher's own shape
# guard failed there while every Windows worktree passed it. `cmd.exe` can silently skip the body of a
# lone-LF batch, so the ending is a property of the shipped artifact, not of the host that cloned it.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
# Shell hooks have no extension, so `* text=auto` + core.autocrlf=true hands the working tree CRLF
# bytes and `sh` mis-parses every line (the reason .githooks/pre-commit ran as a silent no-op until
# 2026-10-10, ERR-261). Hooks must stay LF in the checkout, not just in the object.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
# Large binary routing is policy-controlled; do not silently delete assets.
*.psd filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.zip filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# Owner inbound archives stay plain blobs. Measured 2026-10-21: the four archives already under
# docs/history/owner-inputs/ are stored as full bytes (`i/lf w/-text`), and
# tests/workflow-assistance/test_material_catalog_uses_repository_bytes.py + `owner_material_catalog.py verify`
# hash the archived bytes to prove a last copy survived. Routing a NEW inbound zip to LFS would hand those
# readers a pointer file instead of the ZIP bytes wherever `lfs: true` is not set on the checkout — the ERR-283
# shape, where a green local run and a red foreign host were the same commit. Largest inbound archive is
# 94 kB, so LFS buys nothing here.
docs/history/owner-inputs/**/*.zip -filter -diff -text
# Immutable 2026-10-09 input/snapshot bytes: preserve original line endings and hashes.
taskpacks/history/UI-PRIORITY-CUTOVER-20261009/original-tree/** -text -diff
docs/history/owner-inputs/20261009/ui-readable/** -text -diff
docs/history/owner-inputs/20261009/final-readable/** -text -diff
# Lossless owner-source bytes; authored indexes/registries outside originals remain text.
docs/history/owner-inputs/record-20261009/originals/** -text -diff
